{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9a4a37a687760093", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# BigCodec: Pushing the Limits of Low-Bitrate Neural Speech Codec\narXiv: 2409.05377\nAuthors: Detai Xin, Xu Tan, Shinnosuke Takamichi, Hiroshi Saruwatari\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We introduce BigCodec, a low-bitrate neural speech codec with a bitrate of 1.04 kbps that scales up the model size to 159M parameters and employs a single codebook with 8192 codes to avoid the extra complexity of multiple codebooks.\n  2. We demonstrate through comprehensive objective and subjective evaluations that BigCodec significantly outperforms previous low-bitrate codecs and achieves objective performance comparable to popular codecs operating at 4-6 times higher bitrates while delivering even better subjective perceptual quality than the ground truth.\n  3. We validate the contributions of model scale-up and specific design choices through ablation studies and evaluate BigCodec's generalization ability on unseen languages and its inference efficiency.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "058a4cad-00f1-423a-87d6-78b4fbfd35a6", "uuid": "7008e616-b033-482f-bbc2-649997dd275f", "timestamp": "2026-08-03T07:46:36.253Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# BigCodec: Pushing the Limits of Low-Bitrate Neural Speech Codec\narXiv: 2409.05377\nAuthors: Detai Xin, Xu Tan, Shinnosuke Takamichi, Hiroshi Saruwatari\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We introduce BigCodec, a low-bitrate neural speech codec with a bitrate of 1.04 kbps that scales up the model size to 159M parameters and employs a single codebook with 8192 codes to avoid the extra complexity of multiple codebooks.\n  2. We demonstrate through comprehensive objective and subjective evaluations that BigCodec significantly outperforms previous low-bitrate codecs and achieves objective performance comparable to popular codecs operating at 4-6 times higher bitrates while delivering even better subjective perceptual quality than the ground truth.\n  3. We validate the contributions of model scale-up and specific design choices through ablation studies and evaluate BigCodec's generalization ability on unseen languages and its inference efficiency.\n\nTags: 压缩, 压缩/量化-VQ, 压缩/语义声学-声学", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
