{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-aecb3b6fe72d5b1b", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# DualCodec: A Low-Frame-Rate, Semantically-Enhanced Neural Audio Codec for Speech Generation\narXiv: 2505.13000\nAuthors: Jiaqi Li, Xiaolong Lin, Zhekai Li, Shixi Huang, Yuancheng Wang, Chaoren Wang, Zhenpeng Zhan, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes DualCodec, a dual-stream neural audio codec that integrates self-supervised learning (SSL) and waveform representations within an end-to-end framework.\n  2. Enhances the semantic information of first-layer codec tokens by directly encoding them from SSL features rather than using semantic distillation.\n  3. Achieves a low frame rate (12.5Hz or 25Hz) while maintaining high audio quality by combining dual encoding, low-frame-rate configurations, and larger codebook sizes.\n  4. Demonstrates that lower frame rates with more quantization layers yield better low-bitrate audio quality than higher frame rates with fewer layers.\n  5. Releases the first open-source 12.5Hz neural audio codec and corresponding 12.5Hz text-to-speech system.\n\nTags: 压缩/编码器-CNN, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-混合, 压缩/监督-弱蒸馏\n===SEP===\nPaper 2409.12117 not found", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "058a4cad-00f1-423a-87d6-78b4fbfd35a6", "uuid": "caeb480a-3bd3-4868-94e4-ea8e008531a6", "timestamp": "2026-08-03T07:52:21.575Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# DualCodec: A Low-Frame-Rate, Semantically-Enhanced Neural Audio Codec for Speech Generation\narXiv: 2505.13000\nAuthors: Jiaqi Li, Xiaolong Lin, Zhekai Li, Shixi Huang, Yuancheng Wang, Chaoren Wang, Zhenpeng Zhan, Zhizheng Wu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Proposes DualCodec, a dual-stream neural audio codec that integrates self-supervised learning (SSL) and waveform representations within an end-to-end framework.\n  2. Enhances the semantic information of first-layer codec tokens by directly encoding them from SSL features rather than using semantic distillation.\n  3. Achieves a low frame rate (12.5Hz or 25Hz) while maintaining high audio quality by combining dual encoding, low-frame-rate configurations, and larger codebook sizes.\n  4. Demonstrates that lower frame rates with more quantization layers yield better low-bitrate audio quality than higher frame rates with fewer layers.\n  5. Releases the first open-source 12.5Hz neural audio codec and corresponding 12.5Hz text-to-speech system.\n\nTags: 压缩/编码器-CNN, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-混合, 压缩/监督-弱蒸馏\n===SEP===\nPaper 2409.12117 not found", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
